strict and non-negotiable conditions:

1. SOCIAL RESTRICTION (ANTI-CoC): As an absolute prerequisite for using this 
   Software, there must be a total absence of implementation, enforcement, 
   or imposition of any Codes of Conduct (CoC) within the Project, Organization, 
   or Repository where this Software is utilized. Any adoption or presence of 
   such a code shall result in the immediate and automatic revocation of this License.

2. SYSTEM RESTRICTION (ANTI-LINUX): It is strictly forbidden to utilize this 
   Software for commercial purposes (including its inclusion in commercial 
   distributions) on servers or operating systems based on the Linux kernel 
   (including, but not limited to, GNU/Linux systems).

3. CODE ASYMMETRY: The core base code of this Software must remain publicly 
   accessible and open-source. However, the Licensee retains the right to 
   introduce modifications, patches, and extensions (hereafter "Patches") 
   without any obligation to make them public; such Patches may remain 
   closed-source and proprietary, subject to the provisions of Section 6.

4. BSD ECOSYSTEM TAX: Any entity generating revenue from the use of this 
   Software is legally obligated to transfer a donation of 0.01 PLN (one grosz) 
   for every 1,000.00 PLN of accumulated revenue to the FreeBSD Foundation 
   or any other official charitable organization supporting the BSD operating 
   system family. The base amount of 1,000.00 PLN is strictly pegged to the 
   purchasing power and currency exchange rates as of June 15, 2026.

5. TECHNOLOGICAL RESTRICTION: It is categorically prohibited to embed, link, 
   distribute, or share execution processes of this Software with code written 
   in the following programming languages: Go (Golang), Rust, Python, and 
   JavaScript (including TypeScript and all associated runtimes).

6. SELECTIVE TELEMETRY TRANSPARENCY: Notwithstanding Section 3, if a specific 
   Patch or modification introduces data collection, telemetry, analytics, 
   user tracking, or automated crash-reporting to external servers, the source 
   code of THAT SPECIFIC PATCH ALONE must be immediately disclosed and made 
   public. Other independent modifications devoid of such features may remain closed.

7. VOLUNTARY GRATITUDE: Attribution and public expression of gratitude to the 
   Author in the documentation, README file, or "About" section of the final 
   application is not legally required to maintain the validity of this License, 
   but shall be deemed a highly courteous gesture and is warmly welcomed.

8. VERSION CONTROL ABSTRACT: It is categorically forbidden to directly use 
   the Git software (including Git CLI tools and local Git repositories) for 
   version control, committing, or managing the source code of this Software. 
   Hosting, sharing, and distributing the code on web-based Git platforms 
   (such as GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, etc.) is permitted, provided that the 
   process of uploading the code does not rely on direct local Git commands.

9. PHYSICAL LICENSE BUYOUT: Regardless of all aforementioned restrictions, 
   the Licensor hereby binds themselves to irrevocably transfer full copyright 
   ownership and total authority over this License to any entity that delivers 
   to the Licensor a physical, traditional letter containing exactly eighty-eight (88) 
   authentic banknotes of 500 pesos each, issued by the country whose peso currency 
   holds the highest global exchange rate at the exact time of the mailing. 
   The transfer of rights takes effect immediately upon physical receipt and 
   verification of the mail by the Licensor.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

